body:
[A10] Assignment for [A670] on #780. The lane is from dev a032c6d6. Dev will move when #779, #777 and #778 merge; merge dev into this branch when asked.

Do exactly the issue's Required list:
1. Bump the protocol-processor gitlink to ed2118035e4cec76fb1b59cfbf8a053aeacc8af8, resolved with git rev-parse inside the submodule after checking its toplevel and origin. FPGA-gPTP stays at 55680bff.
2. `git grep` milan-fpga for every expectation of NOT_IMPLEMENTED or status 1 for a wrong-type GET_AVB_INFO: tests, models, docs, the compliance matrix and the testing guide. Update each to NOT_SUPPORTED (11), citing IEEE 1722.1-2021 Table 7-141 and processor #200.
3. The gates:
   - the full sweep as 4 parallel shard units;
   - milan_dp;
   - the firmware gate set;
   - the rtl-fast replica, including `cd tests && behave --no-capture -f plain`;
   - Yosys, lint, and the docs gates under make 4.3;
   - route-1x1, ooc-1x1 and ooc-8x8 against the current (eleventh) record, one Vivado run at a time.
4. Update the submodule adoption table, the CHANGELOG and the parent-visible list.

STOP if any LUT, FF or slice tolerance is exceeded, or if a consumer gate fails for a reason other than the status change. Post TAKEN, then REVIEW READY or STOP, on #780.
